{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a3aa8a459a11198d","name":"Zero-Gravity Stormtrooper Armor","source":{"id":"source:reference-a3aa8a459a11198d","title":"Zero-Gravity Stormtrooper Armor","revision":20834,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:36:33Z","sha256":"a4e2637c21fa13f4e176777b7073c800a1b6fee12fd532b64012650a41e7adcd","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20834","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Zero-Gravity%20Stormtrooper%20Armor&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a3aa8a459a11198d","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed to enable the Emperor's elite ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spacetroopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spacetroopers"}," to cut their way through the hull of an enemy vessel during space combat, Zero-Gravity Stormtrooper Armor is essentially a small ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},". Over two meters tall and twice as wide as a normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},", Zero-Gravity Armor has earned the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spacetroopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spacetroopers"}," the nickname \"Walking Tanks.\" There have been several versions of the Zero-Gravity Armor; the first two iterations were large, bulky, and really more like small ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},". The armor presented here is the lighter Spacetrooper Armor, which was developed after the Mark II version of the armor came into service. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["All Zero-Gravity Stormtrooper Armor incorporates shoulder-mounted ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grenade Launchers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grenade_Launchers"}," (loaded with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Grenades"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Grenades"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun Grenades"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun_Grenades"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gas Grenades"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gas_Grenades"},"), a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:ae1584087cb7657b"},", and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Miniature Proton Torpedo Launcher"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Miniature_Proton_Torpedo_Launcher","referenceId":"reference:cbf39215b667fa67"},". The gauntlets are fitted with either rotating blades or laser cutters, enabling ",{"tag":"a","children":["Spacetroopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Spacetroopers"}," to cut through the hulls of enemy craft. The armor is currently manufactured only for Medium creatures, and increases the wearer's size to Large.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Routine maneuvers in Zero-Gravity Spacetrooper Armor do not require a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check, but the wearer must make a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check to perform any maneuver more complicated than simple movement. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Type:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Armor","referenceId":"reference:4bc2d20a5687b54f"}," \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 21,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},":"]}," +9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},":"]}," +3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Maximum ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," Bonus:"]}," +0\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 38 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
